    <h1>Privacy Policy for UChat</h1>
    <p class="effective-date">Effective Date: August 2, 2026</p>
  </header>

  <p>UChat ("we," "our," or "us") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal data you share with us. This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, and handle your information when you use our mobile application, UChat.</p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

  <h3>A. Authentication Data</h3>
  <p>When you sign in using Email, Google, or Phone Number, we collect basic profile information through Firebase Authentication:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email Login:</strong> Email address and password (encrypted).</li>
    <li><strong>Google Login:</strong> Google profile information (name, email, profile picture).</li>
    <li><strong>Phone Login:</strong> Mobile phone number and verification codes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>B. Communication Content</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> We process your text messages to deliver them to your chat partners in real time.</li>
    <li><strong>Media:</strong> Images, videos, and voice recordings you send are processed for transmission only and are not permanently stored on our servers.</li>
    <li><strong>Local Storage:</strong> Your chat history and media are stored exclusively on your device in a secure local database (Room) for your convenience.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>C. Permissions &amp; Device Data</h3>
  <p>To provide our features, the app requests the following permissions:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Microphone (RECORD_AUDIO):</strong> To allow you to record and send voice messages.</li>
    <li><strong>Contacts (READ_CONTACTS):</strong> To allow you to select and share specific contacts with others. We do NOT upload your entire contact list to our servers.</li>
    <li><strong>Camera/Storage:</strong> To capture and share photos or videos from your gallery.</li>
    <li><strong>Internet:</strong> To transmit messages in real-time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service Delivery:</strong> To operate and maintain the messaging features.</li>
    <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> To verify your identity and secure your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Real-time Features:</strong> To deliver messages instantly via secure WebSocket connections.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Data Storage and Security</h2>
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <p><strong>Local-Only Storage:</strong> Your messages, media, and chat history are stored exclusively on your device and are never transmitted to or permanently stored on our servers. Our relay server (Node.js + Socket.io) only facilitates real-time message delivery between users and does not retain message content after delivery.</p>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Real-time Transmission:</strong> Data in transit is handled through secure socket layers.</li>
    <li><strong>Third-Party Services:</strong> We use Firebase for authentication and infrastructure. These services maintain their own high-level security standards.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>Our app uses the following third-party integrations:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Firebase Authentication:</strong> For secure login.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Play Services:</strong> For core app functionality.</li>
    <li><strong>Socket.io:</strong> For real-time messaging infrastructure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Your Choices &amp; Data Control</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Local-Only Storage:</strong> All your chat messages, media, and history are stored exclusively on your device using a local Room database. We do not store your message content on any external server.</li>
    <li><strong>Account Deletion:</strong> You can delete your account at any time through the app's Settings &gt; Delete Account option. This will permanently remove your authentication data from our systems.</li>
    <li><strong>Automatic Data Removal:</strong> Since all data is stored locally, uninstalling the app from your device will permanently erase all your chat history, media, and local data.</li>
    <li><strong>Clearing History:</strong> You can also use the "Clear Chat" feature to delete specific conversations without uninstalling the app.</li>
    <li><strong>Permission Control:</strong> You can revoke app permissions (Microphone, Contacts, etc.) at any time through your device settings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Account &amp; Data Deletion</h2>
  <p>You may delete your account and all associated authentication data at any time via <strong>Settings &gt; Delete Account</strong> within the app. Since all chat data is stored locally on your device, uninstalling the app will also permanently delete all local content, including messages and media.</p>

  <h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>UChat is not intended for children under the age of 13 (or 16 in the European Union). We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.</p>

  <h2>8. Data We Do Not Sell</h2>
  <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties for marketing or any other purposes.</p>

  <h2>9. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>Authentication data (such as your email or phone number) is retained only as long as your account remains active. Once you delete your account, this data is permanently removed from our systems. Chat content is never stored on our servers and exists only locally on your device.</p>

  <h2>10. International Users</h2>
  <p>If you are located in the European Union, United Kingdom, or California, you may have additional rights regarding your personal data under applicable laws such as the GDPR or CCPA, including the right to access, correct, or request deletion of your data.</p>

  <h2>11. Updates to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page along with an updated effective date.</p>

